Package: SIMP
Title: Symplectic Integrators for Monte-Carlo Proposals
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", , "gilles.colling051@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Gilles Colling [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Gilles Colling <gilles.colling051@gmail.com>
Description: Symplectic integration of separable Hamiltonian systems and the
    Hamiltonian Monte Carlo proposals built on them. The integrators are
    splitting schemes: an alternating sequence of position and momentum
    updates whose coefficients define the method. Leapfrog and the Yoshida
    order 4, 6, and 8 members are generated from a single triple-jump
    composition, so the whole family shares one stepper and one coefficient
    source. The stepper is a header-only, scalar-templated C++ core that other
    packages can link against, so it runs under automatic differentiation as
    well as plain double precision.
